public final class Level2Controller extends BaseLevelController{protected int level(){return 2;}protected String titleText(){return "UNIVERSAL SOLVENT";}protected String objectiveText(){return "Orient polar water molecules to form hydration shells.";}protected String instructionText(){return "For Na⁺ select oxygen inward; for Cl⁻ select hydrogen inward.";}protected List<String> challengeItems(){return List.of("Na⁺","Oδ− inward","Cl⁻","Hδ+ inward");}protected List<Integer> correctOrder(){return List.of(0,1,2,3);}protected String quizPrompt(){return "Why does sodium chloride dissolve in water?";}protected List<String> quizChoices(){return List.of("Salt evaporates","Hydration shells separate the ions","Water is non-polar","NaCl becomes covalent");}protected int quizCorrect(){return 1;}protected String explanation(){return "Ion–dipole attractions form hydration shells and pull Na⁺ and Cl⁻ apart.";}}
